well another week another major news  story related to ufos the new york times  is reporting  about the contents of a soon to be  released pentagon investigation  into the ufo mystery yeah the times says  the report to congress will leave  open the question of whether some ufos  are indeed alien  spacecraft george knapp has our story  [Music]  the initial new york times headline  declared government finds no evidence  ufos are alien spacecraft then clarified  things in a later  headline that added the government can't  rule out alien tech  either a more accurate headline could  have been pentagon says we don't know  what ufos are  or the real news in the story pentagon  says ufos are not secret american  technology  unnamed officials who've seen a  classified report not yet provided to  congress  told the times the report analyzes 120  ufo incidents  from over the past 13 years much of the  evidence was previously compiled into a  briefing document  produced by the uap task force a report  that includes  startling images of craft considered to  be true  unknowns a few images and videos from  that report have already been made  public by mystery wire  and filmmaker jeremy corbell photos  taken by navy pilots off the east coast  and videos recorded by the navy off the  west coast  unknown objects that surrounded nine  warships in july 2019  two other incidents evaluated by the uap  task force  the so-called gimbal ufo event off  florida in 2015  and the tic tac incident off southern  california in 2004  the time says the unreleased report  leaves open the question of whether the  amazing technology  might belong to a foreign adversary  david fravor the pilot who chased the  tic tac  shared his opinions with us in 2019  if you'd asked me in 2004 i didn't know  my thing is it's now almost 15 years  later and that technology is still there  no one has figured it out or no one has  seen it  you can hide stuff you can hide stuff  for a long time but hiding stuff for 15  years  is i think it gets harder and harder if  the time story is accurate then the  upcoming ufo report will be amazingly  similar to this  assessment written by an american  general back in 1947  which basically said these things are  real but we don't know whose they  are the biggest news in the time story  is that the report essentially will rule  out the possibility  that secret american military tech is  responsible for the most notable ufo  incidents  former nevada senator harry reid who  co-sponsored the predecessor program to  the uap  task force has said all along that the  russians and chinese  are also studying the ufo mystery for  the same reason we are  meaning they're not ours lou elizondo  who spent 10 years as head of the atip  ufo investigation says the technology  seen by u.s  pilots is beyond anything known on earth  he told mystery wire the u.s  russia and china are all in the same  boat  we may be dealing with something here  that we we really don't understand  because if we're having the same problem  that russia is in other countries  then then chances are this is a a a  this is a topic that is a mutual concern  and interest for  for for more than just the united states  in fact it would paint the picture that  this is not a u.s phenomenon at all but  this is rather a global phenomenon  the uap report is due in congress by  june 25th  what we don't know yet is what access  the task force  had to classified files and materials  stashed in dark corners of the pentagon  or cia  after 70 years of secrecy did the task  force crack that veil  in a mere six months retired  intelligence officer colonel john  alexander  doubts it well i think there's two  issues the most serious pushback you're  not going to see  that's going to happen behind the  curtain if you will  so it's where they say hell no we won't  go you know i'm not going to provide the  data  george knapp 8 news now well george adds  that the biggest difference between the  upcoming ufo report and previous  statements provided by the pentagon  is that the military is no longer being  dismissive of ufos  or trying to brush them off as swamp gas  or weather balloons
 

